{'symbol': 'TYL', 'date': '2019-10-29 22:30:00', 'title': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. (NYSE:TYL) ACQUIRED CERTAIN ASSETS OF COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES FOR $19 MILLION.', 'text': 'TYLER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. (NYSE:TYL) ACQUIRED CERTAIN ASSETS OF COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES FOR $19 MILLION ON OCTOBER 30, 2019. THE TOTAL PURCHASE PRICE WAS APPROXIMATELY $19 MILLION IN CASH, SUBJECT TO CERTAIN POST-CLOSING ADJUSTMENTS. COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES WILL COMPLEMENT AND ELEVATE TYLER’S SOFTWARE OFFERINGS FOR DOMESTIC AND INTERNATIONAL COURT CLIENTS. COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES MANAGEMENT AND STAFF WILL BECOME PART OF TYLER’S COURTS & JUSTICE DIVISION AND ITS CURRENT EMPLOYEES ARE EXPECTED TO REMAIN IN THE CURRENT OFFICE SPACE IN VANCOUVER. SCOTT KERR IS THE CO-FOUNDER OF COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES AND HE WILL LEAD THE BUSINESS UNIT AS GENERAL MANAGER.\nTYLER TECHNOLOGIES, INC. COMPLETED THE ACQUISITION OF CERTAIN ASSETS OF COURTHOUSE TECHNOLOGIES ON OCTOBER 30, 2019.\n'}